# sgo.build (schema: see core/sgo.build). wata-fb is an APP over core + json +
# wataclient (the portable client core) that rides a cgo Go dep (go-pkgs/audio,
# static opus/tinyalsa libs on a cgo cross-build).
mode app
emitname wata-fb
binname wata-fb
gomod watafb
optreport
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/audio go-pkgs/audio cgo
# The embedded iroh transport (plan 0013): a plain Go dep; its REAL cgo build
# is opt-in (darwin + `-tags iroh`), so ordinary builds ride its pure-Go stub.
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/irohnet go-pkgs/irohnet
# The per-request HTTP deadline (plan 0022): a plain Go dep for the one
# net/http.Client field the bound facade does not carry.
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/httpc go-pkgs/httpc
# The enrolment QR (plan 0014): a thin local adapter (go-pkgs/qr) over
# rsc.io/qr, which it requires as an ORDINARY fetched Go dependency —
# `godep` names a local dir, so an upstream package rides in through one.
# Pure Go, no build tag.
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/qr go-pkgs/qr
# The boot-time type rasteriser (plan 0077 stage 1): strikes for the role-
# aware VLabel painter, over golang.org/x/image (an ordinary fetched dep, the
# same plan-0014 pattern as qr). Pure Go, no build tag.
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/strikes go-pkgs/strikes
# The Gio window (plan 0023 M2): the desktop/phone shell that hosts this same
# frame loop. Gio compiles in only with the `gioshell` build tag (just
# phone-blit); ordinary builds — including the armv7 device cross-build — ride
# its window-free stub, so no build here grows a window toolkit by default.
godep github.com/adriaanm/wata/go-pkgs/gioshell go-pkgs/gioshell
